{
  "$comment": [
    "Proposed tr additions for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns.tr per rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (M3, tr). Not merged: the lead merges them (Wave 2 notes).",
    "Every claims-lint rule with per-locale patterns is covered except selection-translate and jargon, which already have tr (seçerek / metni seç; hizalama). Rules whose only key is '*' (io-home, engine-claim) are skipped.",
    "Patterns are matched like L-14 (flags 'iu', placeholders filled). Word edges are written as explicit (?<!\\p{L}) / (?!\\p{L}), so they hold with or without the Unicode-aware \\w / \\W / \\b of bb689eb. The /iu flags do not fold the Turkish capital İ (U+0130) to i, so words that start with İ/i are written [İi]….",
    "keywordMap.seOwned is meant to replace the current seOwned.tr [\"İngilizce öğren\"] (same intent; [İi] also catches lower-case and ASCII spellings). seOwnedLead is applied to every H2 of every locale (validate-dist D-8), so its tr pattern only matches Turkish openings. \"parça çıkarma\" (the app name of Chunk Extraction) enforces R83 in the title / H1 / description / OG zone.",
    "Tested in the private copy (scratchpad wbw-m3-tr): 0 hits on src/locales/tr.json; at least one hit per rule on the counter-example sentences listed in docs/redesign-2026/ops/m3/tr-qa.md (appendix A)."
  ],
